venv/

# Agent session bootstrap — injected into the checkout per session, not
# repository content. .claude/rules is a symlink into the governance clone
# (an absolute machine path) and .claude/skills is a projection of the
# governance skill library, so committing either would duplicate the
# governance SSOT and hardcode a machine path. .mcp.json is environment
# specific. A repo that later wants its own tracked Claude config can
# un-ignore the specific paths it owns.
/.claude/
/.mcp.json

# Governance session wiring and gate receipts — generated per session by the
# L9 governance bootstrap and the `make pr` gate, not repository content.
# .cursor-commands is a symlink into the governance clone (an absolute machine
# path), and .l9/pr + .l9/autonomy are per-run gate/L4/kernel receipts that
# describe one machine's run. .l9/deployment.yaml IS repository content and
# stays tracked, so these are scoped rather than ignoring /.l9/ wholesale.
/.cursor-commands
/.cursor/
/.l9/pr/
/.l9/autonomy/
